<title>BELGIUM: Belgian CCB, French CLF JV baptised Dexia.</title>
<headline>Belgian CCB, French CLF JV baptised Dexia.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's second largest bank Credit Communal/Gemeentekrediet (CCB) said on Tuesday the cross-border company that will result from its alliance with France's Credit Local de France (CLF) will be called Dexia.</p>
<p>Dexia will be used as the cross-border group's corporate name. The two operating companies in France and Belgium will keep their present names, CCB said in a statement.</p>
<p>Belgian CCB shareholders are due to vote on the proposed alliance and bourse listing of a part of CCB's capital on October 14.</p>
<p>CLF is already listed.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
